🚽 Test case: #196 -- a struct/union-tagged pointer's initializer is now
🚽 type-checked (PR #248 review, finding 1). Before this fix,
🚽 semantic_visit_declaration() special-cased any declaration whose
🚽 data.op.right is a NODE_STRUCT_DEF type marker and returned before
🚽 ever comparing struct_init_expr's inferred type against the declared
🚽 type -- so `gang Point *pp = &n;` (n a plain rizz) parsed and ran,
🚽 silently aliasing an int as if it were a Point.
gang Point {
    rizz x;
    rizz y;
};

skibidi main {
    rizz n;
    n = 42;
    gang Point *pp = &n;
    yapping("%d", pp.x);
}
